\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Tully-Fisher velocity evolution from $z = 0$ to $z = 4$. The solid green curve is the SST prediction $v(z)/v(0) = [H(z)/H_0]^{0.17}$ with zero free parameters. The shaded band is the $\pm 6.2\%$ geometric uncertainty derived from the tetrahedral-to-spherical aperture correction $(K/\pi )^{1/4}$. The dashed line is the $\Lambda $CDM prediction of no evolution. Colored circles are IFU survey measurements from table~\ref {tab:tf}. The starred point is SINS BX442 at $z = 2.18$, a grand-design spiral rotating 27\% faster than the local Tully-Fisher calibration. All nine measurements fall within the SST prediction band. Data served from the Field Dynamics API.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tf}{{1}{5}{Tully-Fisher velocity evolution from $z = 0$ to $z = 4$. The solid green curve is the SST prediction $v(z)/v(0) = [H(z)/H_0]^{0.17}$ with zero free parameters. The shaded band is the $\pm 6.2\%$ geometric uncertainty derived from the tetrahedral-to-spherical aperture correction $(K/\pi )^{1/4}$. The dashed line is the $\Lambda $CDM prediction of no evolution. Colored circles are IFU survey measurements from table~\ref {tab:tf}. The starred point is SINS BX442 at $z = 2.18$, a grand-design spiral rotating 27\% faster than the local Tully-Fisher calibration. All nine measurements fall within the SST prediction band. Data served from the Field Dynamics API}{figure.1}{}}
