\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The Hubble constant from six independent measurement methods and the GFD prediction. The green diamond is the SST prediction $H_0 = 70.21$~km\,s$^{-1}$\,Mpc$^{-1}$. The shaded band spans 65.9 to 74.6~km\,s$^{-1}$\,Mpc$^{-1}$, the $\pm 6.2\%$ geometric uncertainty from the tetrahedral aperture correction. Blue circles are early-universe measurements. Orange and red circles are late-universe measurements. The pink circle is the gravitational wave standard siren GW170817. All six independent measurements fall within the single GFD prediction band. Data served from the Field Dynamics API.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:h0}{{2}{7}{The Hubble constant from six independent measurement methods and the GFD prediction. The green diamond is the SST prediction $H_0 = 70.21$~km\,s$^{-1}$\,Mpc$^{-1}$. The shaded band spans 65.9 to 74.6~km\,s$^{-1}$\,Mpc$^{-1}$, the $\pm 6.2\%$ geometric uncertainty from the tetrahedral aperture correction. Blue circles are early-universe measurements. Orange and red circles are late-universe measurements. The pink circle is the gravitational wave standard siren GW170817. All six independent measurements fall within the single GFD prediction band. Data served from the Field Dynamics API}{figure.2}{}}
